---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Procrastination Timer"
  description="Procrastination Timer collects no data. Timers and settings stay on your device. What each permission is for, how tips are processed and how this website is hosted."
>
  <section class="page-heading wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
    <h1>
      Private.
      <br />
      <span>By design.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      The short version, exactly as it appears inside the app:
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose">
      <p class="summary-box">
        Procrastination Timer collects no data. There are no accounts, no
        analytics and no ads. Your timers and settings stay on your device. Tips
        are processed by Google Play or the App Store under their own terms, and
        the app never sees your payment details.
      </p>
      <p class="policy-date">Effective 12 September 2026.</p>

      <h2>Who this covers</h2>
      <p>
        Procrastination Timer is a two-stopwatch app for Android 7.0 and later
        and iOS 15 and later, made by {site.author}. This policy explains what
        the app does and does not do with your information, and how this website
        is hosted.
      </p>

      <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        The app keeps your two timers, the labels you give them and your
        settings (theme, timer method, notification preference) in its private
        storage on your device so they are there when you come back. This
        information is never sent anywhere, and there is no account, so there is
        nothing about you stored on a server that could need deleting. Resetting
        the timers clears the totals, and uninstalling the app removes
        everything.
      </p>

      <h2>How the timers run in the background</h2>
      <p>
        The app records the moment you tap a side and works the totals out from
        the clock. It does not run a tracking service, does not use your
        location or sensors, and does not read anything else on your phone.
      </p>

      <h2>Permissions and why the app asks for them</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Notifications</strong> (Android: POST_NOTIFICATIONS, and
          POST_PROMOTED_NOTIFICATIONS on Android 16 and later). Shows the
          running timer in the notification shade, as a Live Update where
          supported, and tells you when a Pomodoro, 52/17 or 112/26 block ends.
          On iPhone the app asks for notification permission for the same
          block-end alerts.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Exact alarms</strong> (Android: SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM on
          Android 12 and earlier, USE_EXACT_ALARM afterwards). Lets a block-end
          alert arrive at the exact moment the block finishes, even when the
          phone is dozing. Alarms are only scheduled while a timer method is on.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Start after reboot</strong> (Android: RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED).
          Restores the timer notification and any pending block-end alarm after
          the phone restarts or the app is updated.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Internet</strong> (Android: INTERNET and
          ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE). Added by the Google Play billing library so the
          optional tip jar can talk to the store. The app itself makes no
          network requests.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>None of these permissions gives the app access to personal data.</p>

      <h2>Tip jar purchases</h2>
      <p>
        The app is free and nothing is locked. If you choose to leave a tip
        (Chocolate, Coffee, Sandwich or Pizza), the purchase is processed
        entirely by Google Play or Apple's App Store under their own terms. The
        app receives only a confirmation that the purchase succeeded and which
        product it was; it never sees your name, email address or payment
        details. Google's and Apple's handling of purchase data is described in
        the{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>{' '}
        and the{' '}
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party code</h2>
      <p>
        The app contains no analytics, advertising or crash-reporting software.
        The only third-party code beyond the app framework is the platform
        billing library needed for the tip jar.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This website uses no visitor analytics, tracking cookies or advertising
        scripts. Fonts and images are served with the site. The live demo on the
        home page runs entirely in your browser and sends nothing anywhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        Links to Google Play may carry a campaign label identifying this website
        and the page you came from. The label contains no personal identifier.
        Google processes store visits under its own policies.
      </p>
      <p>
        The website is hosted on GitHub Pages. Hosting services process the
        information needed to deliver a page, such as your IP address. See the{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
          GitHub General Privacy Statement
        </a>
        .
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The app is suitable for a general audience. Because it collects no data
        from anyone, it collects no data from children.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If the app's behaviour changes in a way that affects your privacy, this
        page will be updated and the effective date above revised.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
